{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/542171-union-write-up-for-beast","id":542171,"title":"Union Write up for Beast","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-05T21:35:41-07:00","id":542171,"title":"Union Write up for Beast","content":"Something that's been toying with my mind for a bit but here it goes.<br /> <br /> <i>No God nor Man shall take the fruits of our labor.</i> <i>Brothers in Strife, Solidarity in Famine. </i><br /> <br /> So says the Union Card. You've read it twice over and paid no mind to the words. After all, it's just bullshit mantra right to crank out votes right?<br /> <br /> It's only when some nut claiming to have a soul of a monster lays claim to your shop and your union rep drops a twelve gauge in your hands do you understand. You heard whispers about some other nut wanting to do it for free but your the phrase &quot;We'll take him to Selma&quot; and it was dropped. You don't know the context but the meaning is clear. This is a in-house job. The oldest rule. Can't own what you can't defend. The doors open, and the Lair beckons. You fight to hold down a grin. The Beast may have it's Lair but it's housed in your shop and no one knows his shop better than the working man.<br /> <br /> The Union and Begotten have a long and bloody history with each other that can be summed up in a single sentence: ejection by force. By and large, the Union as a whole does not take kindly to Beasts setting up their hunting grounds in their neighborhoods and work areas and once said Beast (or brood of Beasts) are tracked down, they are subject to a harassment campaign ranging from death threats to physical violence targeted at the Beast to get it to leave. The reaction is swift and harsh as Union lore tends to detail that once a Beast has set up an area of their neighborhood (or heaven forbid, their shops), they are nearly damn impossible to dislodge and only solved by the death of the creature or the total destruction of their workplace. This, understandably, keeps members up at night. Say what you want about Vampires. Those monsters can be dislodged with a bit of fire. Beasts.. not so much.<br /> <br /> Contrary to what Beasts claim about the Union, The Union is not a hotbed of Heroes. In fact, Beasts rarely encounter Heroes in their dealings with the Union and those are almost always a third party in the conflict. They typically only realize this after an encounter with the Compact and typically are not in the mood to return.<br /> <br /> Should a Beast should be near a Union meeting in which they are the topic, they will hear a cryptic phrase over and over. &quot;We'll take him to Selma.&quot;<br /> <br /> What does this phrase mean and what is it's context to Heroes?<br /> <br /> Enter Selma, Washington.<br /> <br /> One or two decades back, Selma was a decent town with decent manufacturing hub. it was, of course, unionized complete with threats from management to offshore and counter threats from the workforce to strike. It wasn't great or even good for that matter. But it had a sense of normalcy and beyond dealing with a few Uratha packs, there really wasn't much else to bother anyone. So much so that the Union made it a hub for themselves. Need a place to hide for a few days? Take it to Selma. Need to some weapons to deal with something threatening your workplace? Take it to Selma. The town slowly became a backbone for the compact in the Northwest and most likely would've stated that way.<br /> <br /> But atlas, it didn't. A Brood of Begotten infested the plants and feasted on the fear that it caused. Workplaces became unsafe. Management became downright tyrannical. Members were stressed by nightmares of death and decay. People died. Something had to be done.<br /> <br /> And as quickly as the problem started, the &quot;solution&quot; arrived. Men &quot;of courage&quot; arose and offered to take on the Beasts along with the workers. Not seeing anything wrong, the Union voted and agreed.<br /> <br /> The Beasts were slain and Selma still exists, though not in anything that would be recognizable functioning town. The fight concluded with the manufacturing hub destroyed via intentional over-pressurization of certain chemical vats. The headlines would read &quot;overzealous strikers cause plant to explode, terrorism charges expected.&quot; The courts ruled accordingly. Members were hauled up before court and the compact pulled in every favor it had to save face. The &quot;Heroes&quot; of the event were later found beaten to a bloody pulp and hanging dead in their cells, security tapes mysteriously vanished. It took years for the compact to recover from the blow and many cells suffered because of it.<br /> <br /> Selma still exists. It's primary exports is meth, misery, and broken homes. Primary imports are best left unstated. A reminder to the compact of what can happen if they push too hard or decide to let outside help in.<br /> <br /> So now when Beasts show up and Heroes follow, the working man digs a hole for both. One for the Beast that has infested his shop. The other for the Hero that seeks to damage it. One for the God, the other for the Man. Neither shall take the fruits of the working man's labor from him. Solidarity after all, solidarity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 06-06-2015, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T11:45:54-07:00","id":550448,"title":"","content":"This is awesome and i love it. That is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T14:18:15-07:00","id":558720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/542171-union-write-up-for-beast#post542171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So now when Beasts show up and Heroes follow, the working man digs a hole for both. One for the Beast that has infested his shop. The other for the Hero that seeks to damage it. One for the God, the other for the Man. Neither shall take the fruits of the working man's labor from him. Solidarity after all, solidarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3412-doctor-crimson","name":"Doctor Crimson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}